  "feedback_interpretation": "Recent feedback strengthened the distinction between genuine long endpoints in polar or extended families and unsupported tails in compact aromatic, nitrile, and halogenated controls. It also highlighted abrupt or loading-sensitive response curves, especially for extended aromatic and acceptor-rich families. This batch emphasizes local condition and loading contrasts while preserving compact boundary controls.",
  "batch_rationale": "The batch combines strong-condition extrapolation points, loading contrasts, local aldehyde and heteroaromatic neighborhoods, and compact controls. It repairs endpoint underprediction in responsive families, tests whether condition effects are smooth or threshold-like, and limits global overcorrection by sampling weakly interacting aromatic, nitrile, and halogenated scaffolds. These labels should improve Row-distribution generalization by teaching when retention depends on solvent strength, loading, or local graph context."
